  "details": "I have an OLED monitor and I am usually playing VRChat on desktop frequently. I am making a feedback post sooner than later, but options to make the HUD less static and more friendly to OLED screens would be awesome.\n\nSome notable options that would be nice for both customization and for helping OLED monitors:\n\n1. HUD smoothing, similar to how it works in VR, although I understand if this does not work with the new HUD\n\n2. Outlines of the HUD elements, similar to how it works in VR\n\n3. Pixel shifting, similar to how it works in VR\n\nPreviously, these options were able to be enabled for desktop by using regedit, as they were removed from the settings menu at some point. I don't know if the new UI plans to support them, but I really hope that further customization options to keep the UI moving are planned to be added.\n\nRight now, the best option seems to be turning down the opacity and swapping to minimal. This will help, but ultimately any purely static element is still not great to have on an OLED screen for long periods of time.",
